messages.content:
An Amber statement is a LINE. The parser does not continue across a newline, so a lambda body, a `$[...]` conditional or a table literal spread over several lines is several statements -- and each fragment is a syntax error on its own.

    f:{$[x>0;`pos;`neg]}

Everything on one line. If a definition is genuinely too long, split it into named helpers, one per line.
